            <div xml:id="d63">

                <pb facs="0073" n="61" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg61"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/618: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-04T16:00:00+04:00">July 4, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 5—4:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Reference to Legation’s telegram number 19, June 26, 9 p.m. The Director
                    General of the Political Department today raised the question of the airplane
                    incident of June 24 saying that he had been told by the Foreign Minister to
                    request the Legation “to study” the matter with view to fixing responsibility
                    should similar cases arise in the future. He particularly wanted to know whether
                    American Army planes in India operate independently or are under the Indian Army
                    General Staff. In the latter event he intimated the Afghan Government would
                    consider the British Government responsible. He likewise intimated that the
                    Afghan Government desired to fix responsibility for the future before
                    considering the present case closed. At the same time he expressed the
                    satisfaction of the Afghan Government with the prompt and frank expression of
                    regret for the incident transmitted by this Legation.</p>
                <p>Instructions are requested.</p>
                <p>Repeated to New Delhi.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thayer</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
